":", throwing instead of trapping when either is not a vertex.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(depth(a) + depth(b)).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/Trees\/RootedTree\/lowestCommonAncestor(checked:_:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Tree":{"type":"topic","title":"Tree","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Tree","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/tree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tree","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree: a connected, acyclic undirected graph with at least one vertex, so it has exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n − 1 edges, no self-loop and no parallel edges. The invariant is the type: every initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from unchecked input is failable, and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tree"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be mutated."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree"}}}